---
description: Python & FastAPI coding standards
globs: **/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---
- Type hints on all functions. Pydantic v2 / SQLModel models define request/response shapes.
- Use `async def` route handlers; never block the event loop — offload sync SDK calls with `asyncio.to_thread`.
- Structure: routers → services → repositories/models. Business logic lives in services, not in route handlers.
- SQLModel: sessions as context managers; wrap multi-step writes in one transaction; use typed fields/relationships.
- Errors: domain exceptions in services; translate to `HTTPException` with precise status codes at the boundary.
- No bare `except:`; no `print()` — use `logging`.
- Small, single-purpose functions; Python 3.11 features allowed (match, Self, tomllib).
